## Architectural Overview

The **Wellbit System Architecture Guide** provides engineering standards, topology specifications, and deployment conventions across our custom software engineering engagements. Our platforms are architected around loose coupling, strong typing, fault tolerance, and comprehensive observability.

## Layered Topology Model

```
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|                 Edge & Ingress Tier                   |
|     Cloudflare CDN / WAF / Envoy API Gateway (TLS 1.3)|
+-------------------------------------------------------+
                           |
                           v
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|               Application Services Tier               |
|   Containerized Microservices (Node.js, Go, Python)   |
|   Autonomous Agent Workers & Background Task Pools    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
             |                              |
             v                              v
+------------------------+      +------------------------+
|   Event & Cache Tier   |      |    Persistence Tier    |
| Apache Kafka / Redis   |      | PostgreSQL + pgvector  |
+------------------------+      +------------------------+
```

## Infrastructure Standards

- **Containerization:** All services packaged with multi-stage Docker builds, non-root user execution, and minimal base images (Alpine or Distroless).
- **Orchestration:** Managed Kubernetes (EKS / GKE) with Horizontal Pod Autoscalers (HPA) and automated health/readiness probes.
- **Secrets Management:** Zero hardcoded credentials; dynamic secret injection via HashiCorp Vault or Cloud Secret Manager with automated rotation.
- **Monitoring & Telemetry:** OpenTelemetry SDK instrumentation exporting distributed traces and metrics to Prometheus and Grafana.
